  Once you get to expert skill you'll be throwing d4 (average 
2.5) daggers per throw.  Even daggers with no enchantment can do 
a lot of damage on an approaching monster.  (SMG, aka SubMachine 
Gun, is a good handle for a rogue: firing d4 bursts of daggers.)

  I still remember my surprise when the Captain of the Minetown
guard fell to my thrown daggers before reaching melee range. 
And that character was a wizard, not a rogue.

  An early wizard's main goal, besides survival and improving 
armor & pets, is getting a stack of daggers and improving dagger 
skill from scratch.  That's so d3 daggers can be thrown at Expert
skill, near or far, as the early wizard's main weapon.

  Rogues get d4 daggers thrown at Expert level, due to the class
bonus of one extra dagger per throw.  Even at basic skill level 
you'll be throwing d2 daggers per throw as a Rogue.

  Wizards also have to consider whether it's really worth three
skill slots in the early game to advance daggers from "skilled"
to "Expert".   Rogues don't have nearly the incentive to save
skill slots for other weapons and/or spells.  

  Rogues only have three spell schools they can advance in: 
divination, escape, and matter.  All three schools can be 
advanced to "skilled".  Maxing out all three schools would
take six slots.  Even with the five slots necessary to get
from basic to expert in daggers, that doesn't seem like a lot.
(NB: Spell skills just take one "skill slot" to go from "Basic"
to "Skilled", unlike weapons which take two skill slots.)


From: <http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/spl1-343.txt>

"When you start the game, Healers and Monks will have basic 
skill in the healing school, Priests in clerical and Wizards in 
attack and enchantment; you will be unskilled in all other 
schools."

  So a starting Rogue will be unskilled in all spell schools.
For an early Rogue, advancing each of those schools to basic
should be more than adequate.  So that's a total of three slots.



From: <http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/invt-343.txt>

  Rogues start out with:

Rogue
  +0 <racial> short sword
  6 to 15 uncursed +0 <racial> daggers
  +1 leather armor
  uncursed potion of sickness
  uncursed lock pick
  uncursed sack
