  Stealth is nice.  So is searching.

  Two-weapon should probably be avoided early on, in favor of the
best enchanted shield you can find.  You'll be doing your major
damage throwing daggers.  (NB: Wearing a shield doesn't interfere
with throwing daggers.)  

  Remember, too, that you can throw daggers at a monster no 
matter what the range.  Stand next to a blue jelly and kill it 
with d4 thrown daggers per turn.  Or kill a charging mumak by
starting when it's far away.  

  Learn what the range limit is on daggers.  Remember it changes 
with strength.  So every time you "feel stronger" re-calibrate
your dagger range.  I.e.: throw a dagger to see how far it goes.


